WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.667
Here's one,

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:10.233
a picture puzzle!

00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:12.900
Which shape completes the pattern?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:13.433
A.

00:00:13.433 --> 00:00:15.000
A filled square,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.533
B.

00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:17.133
A filled triangle,

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:17.667
C.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.267
An empty circle,

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.300
or D.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.900
A filled circle?

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.967
Five seconds!

00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:29.933
TIME'S UP!

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.800
The answer is...

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.200
D,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.400
a filled circle!

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.800
The rule is the shape gets

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.200
filled in but stays the same

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:38.600
shape,

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.000
so the empty circle becomes a

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:41.800
filled circle.

00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:43.567
Alright,

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.367
a word analogy!

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.800
Finger is to hand,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.200
as toe is to...

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:50.800
what?

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.400
A.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.033
Leg,

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:52.633
B.

00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:53.233
Shoe,

00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:53.833
C.

00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:54.433
Foot,

00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:55.633
or D.

00:00:55.633 --> 00:00:56.233
Nail?

00:00:56.233 --> 00:00:57.433
Five seconds!

00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:04.433
TIME'S UP!

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:05.467
It's...

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:05.800
C,

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.167
foot!

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.300
A finger is part of a

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:08.667
hand,

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.800
so a toe is part of

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.533
a foot.

00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:13.667
It is the whole that the

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.100
small part belongs to.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:16.933
Okay,

00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:18.933
a number series!

00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:19.600
One,

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.233
three,

00:01:20.233 --> 00:01:20.900
nine,

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:21.567
twenty-seven,

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:22.900
and then...

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.900
what comes next?

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:25.567
A.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.233
Fifty-four,

00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:26.867
B.

00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:27.533
Seventy-two,

00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:28.200
C.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:28.867
Eighty-one,

00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:30.200
or D.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:30.867
Ninety?

00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:32.200
Five seconds!

00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:39.167
TIME'S UP!

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.533
The answer is...

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:42.100
C,

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:42.667
eighty-one!

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:46.067
Each number is multiplied by three:

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:46.633
one,

00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:47.200
three,

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:47.767
nine,

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:48.333
twenty-seven,

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:51.767
so twenty-seven times three is eighty-one.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:53.500
Okay,

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.233
a picture puzzle!

00:01:55.233 --> 00:01:58.767
Where does the dot move next?

00:01:58.767 --> 00:01:59.367
A.

00:01:59.367 --> 00:01:59.933
Top-left,

00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:00.533
B.

00:02:00.533 --> 00:02:01.100
Top-right,

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:01.700
C.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:02.300
Center,

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.467
or D.

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:04.033
Bottom-left?

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.233
Five seconds!

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.200
TIME'S UP!

00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:14.433
The answer is...

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:14.933
A,

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:15.467
top-left!

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:18.033
The dot steps clockwise corner

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:19.100
to corner:

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:19.600
top-right,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.133
bottom-right,

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:20.633
bottom-left,

00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:23.733
so the next corner is top-left.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:25.567
Alright!

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:28.867
Which one does NOT belong?

00:02:28.867 --> 00:02:29.533
A.

00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:30.200
Road,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:30.867
B.

00:02:30.867 --> 00:02:31.533
Car,

00:02:31.533 --> 00:02:32.200
C.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:32.867
Bus,

00:02:32.867 --> 00:02:34.200
or D.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:34.867
Train?

00:02:34.867 --> 00:02:36.167
Five seconds!

00:02:41.967 --> 00:02:43.167
TIME'S UP!

00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:44.233
It's...

00:02:44.233 --> 00:02:44.633
A,

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:45.067
road!

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:45.867
A car,

00:02:45.867 --> 00:02:46.267
bus,

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.700
and train are all vehicles that

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:49.533
carry people.

00:02:49.533 --> 00:02:51.967
A road is what they drive

00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:52.367
on,

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:54.400
so it does not belong.

00:02:55.533 --> 00:02:56.733
Here's one,

00:02:56.733 --> 00:02:58.567
a number series!

00:02:58.567 --> 00:02:59.167
Four,

00:02:59.167 --> 00:02:59.767
five,

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:00.367
seven,

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:01.000
ten,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:01.600
fourteen,

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.800
and then...

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.633
what comes next?

00:03:04.633 --> 00:03:05.233
A.

00:03:05.233 --> 00:03:05.833
Eighteen,

00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:06.433
B.

00:03:06.433 --> 00:03:07.067
Nineteen,

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:07.667
C.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:08.267
Twenty,

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.467
or D.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:10.067
Seventeen?

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.300
Five seconds!

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.267
TIME'S UP!

00:03:18.933 --> 00:03:20.600
The answer is...

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.133
B,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:21.700
nineteen!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.467
The gaps grow by one:

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.567
plus one,

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:26.133
two,

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:26.667
three,

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:27.233
four,

00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:28.900
then plus five.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.200
So fourteen plus five is nineteen.

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:34.433
Here's one,

00:03:34.433 --> 00:03:36.033
a shape puzzle!

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.167
Which shape comes next?

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:38.700
A.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.767
A circle,

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:40.300
B.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.367
A hexagon,

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:41.900
C.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.967
A square,

00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:44.033
or D.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.100
An octagon?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.167
Five seconds!

00:03:51.967 --> 00:03:53.167
TIME'S UP!

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.300
The answer is...

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:55.767
B,

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:56.767
a hexagon!

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:59.667
The sides count up by one:

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:00.633
triangle three,

00:04:00.633 --> 00:04:01.600
square four,

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.600
pentagon five,

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.500
so next is the hexagon with

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.467
six sides.

00:04:07.633 --> 00:04:08.200
Alright,

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.933
a number analogy!

00:04:09.933 --> 00:04:11.667
One makes three,

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.400
two makes six,

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.133
three makes nine,

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:16.867
so four makes...

00:04:16.867 --> 00:04:17.433
what?

00:04:17.433 --> 00:04:18.033
A.

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:18.600
Seven,

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.167
B.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:19.767
Twelve,

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:20.333
C.

00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:20.900
Ten,

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.067
or D.

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:22.633
Fifteen?

00:04:22.633 --> 00:04:23.800
Five seconds!

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:30.767
TIME'S UP!

00:04:31.433 --> 00:04:31.933
It's...

00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:32.433
B,

00:04:32.433 --> 00:04:32.933
twelve!

00:04:32.933 --> 00:04:35.900
Each number is multiplied by three:

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.400
four times three is twelve.

00:04:39.533 --> 00:04:41.167
Check this out,

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:43.367
fill in the blank!

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:46.100
The rain poured all day,

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:49.367
so the school had to blank

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:52.667
the outdoor games until the next

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:53.200
weekend.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:53.733
A.

00:04:53.733 --> 00:04:54.300
Enjoy,

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:54.833
B.

00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:55.400
Paint,

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:55.933
C.

00:04:55.933 --> 00:04:56.467
Count,

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:57.567
or D.

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:58.133
Postpone?

00:04:58.133 --> 00:04:59.200
Five seconds!

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.200
TIME'S UP!

00:05:06.867 --> 00:05:07.300
It's...

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:07.700
D,

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.133
postpone!

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:09.833
Rain stops outdoor games,

00:05:09.833 --> 00:05:12.367
so they had to move them

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:13.200
to later.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.300
Postpone means to put something

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.433
off until a later time.

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:19.667
Here's one,

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.300
a number puzzle,

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.933
and it's sneaky!

00:05:22.933 --> 00:05:26.200
If two plus three makes six,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.900
four plus two makes eight,

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.633
five plus three makes fifteen,

00:05:31.633 --> 00:05:34.367
then six plus two makes...

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:34.900
what?

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:35.433
A.

00:05:35.433 --> 00:05:36.000
Eight,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.533
B.

00:05:36.533 --> 00:05:37.067
Fourteen,

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:37.633
C.

00:05:37.633 --> 00:05:38.167
Twelve,

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:39.267
or D.

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:39.800
Sixteen?

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.900
Five seconds!

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:47.867
TIME'S UP!

00:05:48.533 --> 00:05:49.933
The answer is...

00:05:49.933 --> 00:05:50.400
C,

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:50.867
twelve!

00:05:50.867 --> 00:05:53.667
The plus sign secretly means multiply:

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:56.033
two times three is six,

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:58.367
four times two is eight,

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:01.167
so six times two is twelve.

00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:02.733
So,

00:06:02.733 --> 00:06:04.767
are you smart or fart?

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:07.200
Count up your correct answers to

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.400
find your rank!

00:06:09.567 --> 00:06:09.933
So,

00:06:09.933 --> 00:06:11.367
how did you do?

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:12.833
Comment your score below,

00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:14.300
and subscribe for more!
